  TJJM website overrides, FILE 2 of 2. Same idiom as tjjm-gym-websites: one row per
  gym, tilde + exact gym name + pipe + value + tilde. An EMPTY value BLANKS the link.

  This file exists only because file 1 was approaching the 24 KB Admin API rewrite
  ceiling. The section concatenates both into one string before probing, so the two
  files behave as a single lookup. Precedence note: the probe takes the LAST match,
  so a name present in both files resolves to the entry HERE, in file 2.

  CONTENT: 426 dead or parked links, blanked. Curated states only (Tier A).
  Generated 6 Aug 2026 from a full audit of all 4,282 published outbound links.

  METHOD, stated so the claim dies with the method that produced it:
    1. Harvested every gym link the site publishes, from all 61 rendered region pages.
    2. Browser reachability screen produced 899 candidates. That screen is UNRELIABLE:
       a measured 39 percent false-positive rate (n=18), and it is structurally blind
       to a working link that belongs to somebody else.
    3. Every candidate in the 27 curated states was then re-checked SERVER-SIDE, DNS
       first. NXDOMAIN is conclusive. A blank body is NOT, and was recorded as
       unresolved rather than dead.
    Across 586 verified Tier A links: 414 dead, 12 parked, 9 wrong-entity (blanked in
    file 1), 96 live-and-correct (NOT touched), 55 unresolved (NOT touched).

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE:
    - the 96 the screen flagged that are live and correct. Blanking those would have
      destroyed 96 working links. This is why a screen orders work and never concludes.
    - the 55 that returned an empty body. A fetch failure is not evidence about a
      school. Each is owed one body read.
    - all 300 flagged links in the 34 never-curated regions. Those are a different
      problem: 174 are records named after their own city, and the open question is
      whether the LISTING should exist at all, not whether to blank a URL.

  EVERY NAME HERE WAS CHECKED FOR UNIQUENESS ACROSS ALL 4,630 RECORDS. An override
  matches on NAME ALONE, so a shared name blanks TWO records. 14 names in the corpus
  are used by more than one record; none appear below. DO NOT ADD A ROW WITHOUT
  RUNNING THAT CHECK.

  The gym stays listed with its name, city and map link. Only the bad URL is removed.
  Any row here is reversible by deleting the line.

